{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they","id":886461,"title":"Werewolfs in Germany - Where are they?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-09T11:10:04-07:00","id":886461,"title":"Werewolfs in Germany - Where are they?","content":"If we go by the 500k mortal per Garou ratio which is from the Storyteller's Handbook around 160 German Werwolfes should exist. There is one lvl 3 Caern in the Black Forrest so there could be between 25 and 40 Garou (Get of Fenris) while some Glaswalkers in Frankfurt and that area, but there are still a ton of potential. Should there be more Caerns and/or larger Septs in Germany or are there reasons that would prohibit that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8249,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","user":"Crytash","date":". 05-09-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:53:42-07:00","id":886516,"title":"","content":"I could imagine a high rank, female, Child of Gaia, &quot;Mother Wolf&quot;-kind loupgarou. Settled in K\u00f6ln - Ehrenfeld. After driving off the vampires who ruled this poor part of the city before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","user":"Colognian","date":". 05-10-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:09:50-07:00","id":886595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they#post886461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we go by the 500k mortal per Garou ratio which is from the Storyteller's Handbook around 160 German Werwolfes should exist. There is one lvl 3 Caern in the Black Forrest so there could be between 25 and 40 Garou (Get of Fenris) while some Glaswalkers in Frankfurt and that area, but there are still a ton of potential. Should there be more Caerns and/or larger Septs in Germany or are there reasons that would prohibit that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want more Caerns and larger Septs or even more Garou, go for it. I seldom care about, much less use, the population ratios talked about in books. If I want to have more of Splat X in specific area, I'll put more in. I was once in a MtAs game set in Vancouver where there were a decent number of mages in the city from each Tradition and Convention as well as a few Craft mages and Orphans despite the sliding ratios of Mages-to-Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:43:20-07:00","id":886832,"title":"","content":"The caerns listed in the books are not meant to be the only caerns in an area. They are just the caern(s) the sourcebook wanted to mention. So yes, there are opportunities for additional caerns. There is a frequent poster (Heinrich) on this forum who is from Germany, and no doubt he will comment with his own ideas.<br /> <br /> Europe has a higher population density than North America so there are likely less caerns remaining in Europe, and that is something several sourcebooks elude to.<br /> <br /> I run a historical chronicle in Germany and identified some areas where I believe caerns could function.<br /> <br /> 1) Southern Germany is along the Alps. Somewhere there or in the Alpine foreland, you can probably locate a caern.<br /> <br /> 2) West of the Rhine is the Palatinate Forest which becomes the Vosges Mountains in France. This is a good place for a caern somewhere.<br /> <br /> 3) The Harz Mountains likely would have a caern. Many real world werewolf legends are based there. It is the highest mountain range in Germany. It is also home to the Brocken, the world famous place of witches sabbath during Walpurgisnacht.<br /> <br /> 4) The Thuringian Forest would be another good location.<br /> <br /> 5) Along Germany's border with the Czech Republic might be some good places for a caern. The border is based on the Sudeten Mountains and Bohemian Forest.<br /> <br /> 6) The Teutoburg Forest in Westphalia was home to one of the most famous defeats of the Roman Army. It makes a far better location for the canonical Get of Fenris caern than the Black Forest. In my chronicle, I moved that there and substituted an entirely different caern in the Black Forest.<br /> <br /> 7) I also like the glacial lakes in the Mecklenburg-Vorpormmern area.<br /> <br /> 8) If you are looking for urban caerns, Germany would historically have been a good place for them. Because Germany was politically divided, it never had a central metropole that absorbed everything like London and Paris did for Britain and France. So Germany had a lot of more mid tier cities. Historically, Hamburg, Leipzig, Dresden, Bremen, Lubeck, Magdeburg, and Munich all would have been good places. (Note until the 19th century, Berlin wasn't a major city, although it started becoming important in the 18th century under Frederick the Great). Of course, many of these destroys were either destroyed during the Thirty Years War or World War II, so it is questionable how many urban caerns would have survived. In my game, I have Hamburg and Lubeck as centers of major urban caerns, and Magdeburg a historical one that was destroyed during the Thirty Years War during the Sack of Magdeburg.<br /> <br /> There are also lots of smaller places that could be home to a rank one caern. If you count pre-war Germany, you'd have some potential caern sites in Silesia and Prussia as well.<br /> <br /> Plus you have all sorts of local legends you may want to incorporate. At the town of Bingen on the Rhine, there is a legend of the &quot;Mouse Bishop of Bingen&quot; that tells of a greedy Bishop who wouldn't release grain from storage during a local famine. When the peasants complained, he lured them into a barn and burned them down. Later, a swarm of rats and mice appeared and devoured him. I like the legend so much I placed an important Bone Gnawer caern there.<br /> <br /> The 1 Garou per 500,000 is just a general number. It does not mean that the Garou population is tied to the local human population. It probably doesn't in any local area. A wilderness area with very few people probably have a much smaller ratio (way more Garou than the human population would indicate). In more urban areas with high population density, the local ratio is much, much higher (way fewer Garou than expected based on the ratio). The Get of Fenris are probably more heavily populated in northern Scandinavia than Germany. I'd personally make the ratio in Germany as a whole 1 per million or even 1 per 1.5 million. That would place the Garou population between 54-81. If you want more septs, then keep Garou numbers at sept near the average minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-10-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:35:00-07:00","id":887899,"title":"","content":"(Btw, if the Botanical Garden in Berlin is not a caern, I don't know what is. The experience of the place is just what you'd expect from crossing a bawn line, anyway. Super recommended, and very impressive, at least to me. You'd expect a big European city like that to be hostile territory to most Garou, but that place exists. But since it's a scientific institution, it should probably be Glass Walkers exclusive.<br /> Just had to leave that somewhere.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T02:11:38-07:00","id":887998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they?p=886832#post886832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a frequent poster (Heinrich) on this forum who is from Germany, and no doubt he will comment with his own ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to, but then a bluescreen made my post go to oblivion.<br /> <br /> Basically, what I detailed was how our LARP chronicle has it's NPC septs spread in Germany (as well as Luxembourg and Switzerland).<br /> <br /> Apart from that, there are only a few big cities Berlin with 3,5 million, Hamburg, Munich and Cologne with a million each in Germany. Also the Ruhrpott as a industrial area, formerly a coal mining region, with Dortmund, Bochum and Essen, aswell as D\u00fcsseldorf nearby, are a region with fairly high population. Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker areas, Children of Gaia maybe.<br /> <br /> Besides that, there are woodland regions and farmland. No areas where you can walk for days till you reach a street or village, but areas with fairly low population density. They are good for more traditional tribes. Germany as approximately the size of Montana, but houses about 81 times as much people. So the population density is higher than Maryland's.<br /> <br /> The map at the following link shows the average distance to a highway. It is an indicator, where the more remote areas in Germany are:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.geoportal.de/DE/Geoportal/Karten/karten.html;jsessionid=66469F28069ED16192C9C3EDA61B3562?lang=de&amp;wmcid=69\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geoportal.de/DE/Geoportal/Karten/karten.html;jsessionid=66469F28069ED16192C9C3EDA61B3562?lang=de&amp;wmcid=69\" target=\"_blank\"> Geoportal.de </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.geoportal.de/DE/Geoportal/Karten/karten.html;jsessionid=66469F28069ED16192C9C3EDA61B3562?lang=de&amp;wmcid=69\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.geoportal.de/DE/Geoportal/Karten/karten.html;jsessionid=66469F28069ED16192C9C3EDA61B3562?lang=de&amp;wmcid=69 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:33:52-07:00","id":888177,"title":"","content":"Any mining region or former mining region is going to be... spiritually unpleasant in Werewolf, due to complications like acidification from rainwater mixing with tailings and discarded excavations that happen to contain low pH minerals. Also, BSDs would be loath to pass up a pre-excavated tunnel system, as it saves them the trouble of doing it themselves.<br /> <br /> Population densities are also weird in the WoD. To reinforce the gothic atmosphere, it explicitly has more big cities and fewer small towns, giving it more wilderness, which is often old growth. So you might end up beefing up the numbers in the cities (no pun intended for Hamburg).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:09:37-07:00","id":891394,"title":"","content":"Can't forget the black spirals, who according to botw20 may well be living in formerly vampire run areas. They don't necessarily need tunnels anymore. Might be worth noting they are also considered garou and therefore may be a chunk of the countries population. Hell they could easily be slipping in with the current migration situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:46:44-07:00","id":891767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they?p=891394#post891394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't forget the black spirals, who according to botw20 may well be living in formerly vampire run areas. They don't necessarily need tunnels anymore. Might be worth noting they are also considered garou and therefore may be a chunk of the countries population. Hell they could easily be slipping in with the current migration situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that receiving refugees would be something that they look at as a kind of buffet, not the opportunity to bring in more Dancers to hives that are probably already at full capacity and sending out shock troops to die in order to keep things comfy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:07:59-07:00","id":892126,"title":"","content":"Nah I'd think they'd reinforce the social instability caused by two incompatible cultures coming together, mixed with the lingering hatred of the old war mentality. Seems pretty well of the wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:59:19-07:00","id":892155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they?p=892126#post892126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah I'd think they'd reinforce the social instability caused by two incompatible cultures coming together, mixed with the lingering hatred of the old war mentality. Seems pretty well of the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a buffet. Because after they're done with humans, they don't bury them respectfully...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:13:20-07:00","id":927180,"title":"","content":"Loads of Black Furies in the Schwarzwald of course. Where else do you think it got its name from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:49:06-07:00","id":927236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they?p=886832#post886832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Teutoburg Forest in Westphalia was home to one of the most famous defeats of the Roman Army. It makes a far better location for the canonical Get of Fenris caern...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that it has been <i>specifically</i> stated (Get of Fenris Tribebook, p17) that the defeat of General Varus's three legions there was the result of a single pack of Get cubs undergoing a Rite of Passage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics of War</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't forget the black spirals, who according to botw20 may well be living in formerly vampire run areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also lots of abandoned tunnel complexes that the Nazis used slave labor to dig. Such places probably have spiritual taint that the Dancers would find irresistible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T14:00:27-07:00","id":928901,"title":"","content":"I always hated the 1:500,000 estimate. That would mean that the entire werewolf population on Earth would fit in a small American town. I always played with numbers equivalent to vampires...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:39:47-07:00","id":935856,"title":"","content":"Wasn't the point that they were brutally outnumbered though? And considering that the spirals make up a bulk of the population...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:48:26-07:00","id":936278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/886461-werewolfs-in-germany-where-are-they?p=935856#post935856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't the point that they were brutally outnumbered though? And considering that the spirals make up a bulk of the population...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the bulk. The single largest population, at 10% of all Garou. The bulk i.e. majority of all Garou are still Gaian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":